ceptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire and accompanying x ray of the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 8cm ill defined  soft  red tan area extending to within 0 2cm of the inked margin  adjacent to the thick end of wire  The remaining parenchyma is composed of soft  lobulated  unremarkable adipose tissue  The nodule is submitted in A F  The adjacent parenchyma and firmer areas from the remaining parenchyma are submitted in G O  Resident  Asif Rashid  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT EXCISION  NO GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS LESION THAT IS LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  George S Richardson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST LESION   report_end  , Absent.
