Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 28 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass seen on US and needle biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  FORMING MANY NODULES THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The largest nodule spans at least 2 5cm in greatest dimension in tissue section  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 15 LYMPH NODES AND FOCALLY EXTENDING INTO AXILLARY SOFT TISSUE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 53                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  is an unoriented fibroadipose tissue  measuring 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm  Inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined aggregate of tan white  firm  focally gritty nodules measuring 6 x 2 x 2 5cm  present at multiple resection margins  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary node  is a 6 x 5 x 1cm fragment of fatty adipose tissue  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted entirely in cassettes K through T  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Lawrence T Geoghegan  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION , Absent.
