Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 51 CLINICAL DATA  Strong family history  with right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3   SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS ASSOCIATED WITH INVASIVE COMPONENT  ALL  23  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  The resection margins appear free of tumor  No definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is identified  BREAST  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Labeled  R modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm oriented right breast with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tissue  and overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse with a unremarkable nipple  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm stellate  firm  gritty  white mass located inferomedially  with partial surrounding parenchymal hemorrhage  The mass is 0 3cm from the closest deep margin  and 0 8cm from the overlying anterior margin located just inferior to the skin ellipse  Adjacent  but not contiguous with the mass  there is an approximately 3 0cm area of cystic and focally firm parenchyma  Also noted are other small cysts located away from the tumor  Sections of firm  gritty lesion are in cassettes A C  anterior  superficial  margin in D and E  deep margin in F and G  cystic parenchyma adjacent to mass in H and I  and parenchymal sections away from mass in J and K  The axillary lymph nodes are REMOVED_DATE to 1 4cm in greatest dimension  pink and unremarkable  in cassettes L P  Labeled  L simple mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm oriented RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  , Absent.
